# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"
msgstr "Kumpulkan sebutan operator: gunakan struktur operator {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") can tag each of its terms with a **group index**. The tags carry no meaning of their own: they only say which terms belong together. What the tags *mean* is decided by whatever consumes them. In this package the consumers are the time-evolution gate, which is split into one factor per group, and the randomized qDRIFT pass, which samples whole groups.\n"
msgstr "[`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") boleh menanda setiap sebutannya dengan **indeks kumpulan**. Tanda itu tidak membawa makna tersendiri: ia hanya menyatakan sebutan mana yang tergolong bersama. Apa yang *dimaksudkan* oleh tanda itu ditentukan oleh apa sahaja yang menggunakannya. Dalam pakej ini pengguna ialah gate evolusi masa, yang dibahagikan kepada satu faktor bagi setiap kumpulan, dan pas qDRIFT rawak, yang mensampel keseluruhan kumpulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide shows how to assign groups, how to check the properties a consumer relies on, and how to lay the operator out so that picking a few groups out of a large one stays cheap.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan cara menetapkan kumpulan, cara menyemak sifat yang diharapkan oleh pengguna, dan cara menyusun operator supaya memilih beberapa kumpulan daripada yang besar kekal murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  No automatic grouping strategy ships with this package. You assign the indices yourself, from what you know about your model.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tiada strategi pengelompokan automatik disertakan dengan pakej ini. Anda menetapkan indeks sendiri, berdasarkan apa yang anda ketahui tentang model anda.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assign groups {#assign-groups}"
msgstr "Tetapkan kumpulan {#assign-groups}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The running example is a three-site Bose-Hubbard chain. Each bond contributes a hopping pair, and the on-site interactions form a diagonal piece. The simplest way to build a grouped operator is [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), which takes each term together with its group index as an `(actions, coefficient, group)` triple. You decide the group at the moment you write the term down, when you still know why it belongs there:\n"
msgstr "Contoh yang digunakan ialah rantai Bose-Hubbard tiga tapak. Setiap ikatan menyumbang pasangan lompatan, dan interaksi atas tapak membentuk bahagian pepenjuru. Cara paling mudah untuk membina operator berkumpulan ialah [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), yang menerima setiap sebutan bersama indeks kumpulannya sebagai tiga serangkai `(actions, coefficient, group)`. Anda menentukan kumpulan pada saat anda menulis sebutan itu, ketika anda masih tahu mengapa ia tergolong di situ:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms are stored in the order you give them, so the group indices cannot end up attached to the wrong terms.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan disimpan mengikut tertib yang anda berikan, jadi indeks kumpulan tidak mungkin tersilap dilekatkan pada sebutan yang salah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that already exists has to be grouped after the fact, by assigning the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute. That is where care is needed, because [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not specify the order in which it stores its terms. Writing the list out by position can then attach an index to the wrong term. Derive each index from the term itself instead:\n"
msgstr "Operator yang sudah wujud perlu dikumpulkan selepas itu, dengan menetapkan atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\"). Di situlah perlu berhati-hati, kerana [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") tidak menentukan tertib penyimpanan sebutannya. Menulis senarai mengikut kedudukan kemudian boleh melekatkan indeks pada sebutan yang salah. Sebaliknya, terbitkan setiap indeks daripada sebutan itu sendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of indices has to match the number of terms. Anything else is rejected, because a too-short list would silently drop trailing terms wherever terms are iterated together with their groups:\n"
msgstr "Bilangan indeks mesti sepadan dengan bilangan sebutan. Selain itu ditolak, kerana senarai yang terlalu pendek akan menggugurkan sebutan di hujung secara senyap di mana sahaja sebutan diulang bersama kumpulannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check what the consumer relies on {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"
msgstr "Semak apa yang diharapkan oleh pengguna {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three functions in [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") answer one narrow question each about an existing grouping. None of them says a grouping is “correct”, because correctness is relative to the consumer.\n"
msgstr "Tiga fungsi dalam [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") masing-masing menjawab satu soalan sempit tentang pengelompokan sedia ada. Tiada satu pun menyatakan pengelompokan itu “betul”, kerana kebetulan bergantung pada pengguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Is each group Hermitian?** This is the property that matters most. The time evolution of a group is only unitary if the group is Hermitian, and a lone hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is *not*. Only the pair with its adjoint is Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "**Adakah setiap kumpulan Hermitian?** Ini ialah sifat yang paling penting. Evolusi masa bagi satu kumpulan hanya uniter jika kumpulan itu Hermitian, dan sebutan lompatan tunggal $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ *bukan* Hermitian. Hanya pasangan dengan adjointnya yang Hermitian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A grouping that splits a hopping pair is caught immediately:\n"
msgstr "Pengelompokan yang memecahkan pasangan lompatan dikesan serta-merta:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping terms are caught. The three `True` entries are the on-site terms $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which are Hermitian by themselves. A mode can legitimately repeat within a term, and nothing is dropped for doing so. The flags follow the order of `terms`, which is why each one can be read against the term it describes.\n"
msgstr "Keempat-empat sebutan lompatan (hopping) berjaya dikesan. Tiga entri `True` ialah sebutan pada-tapak $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, yang Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Sesuatu mod boleh berulang secara sah dalam satu sebutan, dan tiada apa yang digugurkan kerana itu. Bendera mengikut susunan `terms`, itulah sebabnya setiap satu boleh dibaca berdasarkan sebutan yang diterangkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Are the coefficients uniform?** A randomized product formula weighs a group by the mean *magnitude* of its coefficients, which is a faithful description of the group only if the magnitudes agree:\n"
msgstr "**Adakah pekalinya seragam?** Formula hasil darab rawak menimbang sesuatu kumpulan mengikut purata *magnitud* pekalinya, yang merupakan huraian setia bagi kumpulan itu hanya jika magnitudnya sepadan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neither check implies the other: uniform coefficients do not make a group Hermitian, and a Hermitian group can mix magnitudes. By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form:\n"
msgstr "Tiada satu pun semakan membawa kepada yang lain: pekali seragam tidak menjadikan sesuatu kumpulan Hermitian, dan kumpulan Hermitian boleh mencampurkan magnitud. Secara lalai magnitud dibandingkan, kerana itulah yang dipuratakan oleh [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). Sepasang Hermitian dengan pekali kompleks mempunyai magnitud yang sama tetapi pekali yang tidak sama, jadi ia hanya memenuhi bentuk lalai:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") is built on [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), which compares an operator with its adjoint after normal ordering. That is an identity of the untruncated algebra, so a group that passes is Hermitian as a bosonic operator. See [Design principles of operator representations](operators#operators-explanation) for how products of ladder operators are ordered and compared.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") dibina di atas [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), yang membandingkan sesuatu pengendali dengan adjointnya selepas penyusunan normal. Itu ialah identiti bagi aljabar tanpa pemangkasan, jadi kumpulan yang lulus adalah Hermitian sebagai pengendali boson. Lihat [Prinsip reka bentuk perwakilan pengendali](operators#operators-explanation) untuk mengetahui bagaimana hasil darab pengendali tangga disusun dan dibandingkan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order the terms by group {#order-the-terms-by-group}"
msgstr "Susun sebutan mengikut kumpulan {#order-the-terms-by-group}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") returns one operator per requested group. When the terms of a group are scattered through the operator, it has to scan every term to find them. When each group forms one contiguous run, it binary-searches the group boundaries instead, so the cost of a lookup follows the number of groups *requested* rather than the number of terms *held*.\n"
msgstr "[`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") mengembalikan satu pengendali bagi setiap kumpulan yang diminta. Apabila sebutan sesuatu kumpulan bertaburan di seluruh pengendali, ia perlu mengimbas setiap sebutan untuk mencarinya. Apabila setiap kumpulan membentuk satu larian bersebelahan, ia mencari sempadan kumpulan secara carian binari, jadi kos setiap carian mengikut bilangan kumpulan yang *diminta* dan bukannya bilangan sebutan yang *disimpan*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") produces that layout. It is a stable sort by group index: the value of the operator does not change, and terms within a group keep their relative order.\n"
msgstr "[`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") menghasilkan susun atur itu. Ia ialah isihan stabil mengikut indeks kumpulan: nilai pengendali tidak berubah, dan sebutan dalam satu kumpulan mengekalkan susunan relatifnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both layouts return the same operators; only the cost differs:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua susun atur mengembalikan pengendali yang sama; hanya kosnya berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
